[
{ type: install
  message: <<EOM

To load mac_do_auto at boot, add to /boot/loader.conf:

    mac_do_auto_load="YES"

Or load it now:

    kldload %%KMODDIR%%/mac_do_auto.ko

Once loaded, members of the wheel group receive implicit privileges.
Adjust the authorized group and scope via sysctl:

    security.mac.autodo.gid=0
    security.mac.autodo.scope=all

To run the autodo-eventd companion daemon (multi-group policy, path
deny list, audit log), install the sample configuration and enable the
service:

    cp %%ETCDIR%%/autodo.conf.sample %%ETCDIR%%/autodo.conf
    sysrc autodo_eventd_enable=YES
    service autodo_eventd start

Policy profiles referenced by "profile = " entries in the config are
installed under %%ETCDIR%%/profiles/.

Note: the kernel module must match the running kernel's MAC framework
version (FreeBSD 15.x); reinstall the package after an OS upgrade to a
new major version.
EOM
}
{ type: upgrade
  maximum_version: "0.3.3"
  message: <<EOM

This version needs a module reload, not just a package upgrade.

autodo-eventd now reads the module's ABI version at startup and exits if
it disagrees, instead of running on against a kernel it cannot
configure.  The module resident in the kernel predates that check, so
the daemon will refuse to start until it is reloaded:

    service autodo_eventd stop
    kldunload mac_do_auto
    kldload mac_do_auto
    service autodo_eventd start

Check the loaded module at any time with:

    autodo-eventd --check-abi

Scope categories now cover every priv(9) constant, which widens what the
named categories grant:

    vfs     also covers UFS, ZFS and NFS administration
    dev     also covers the tty privileges
    system  also covers firmware loading and kenv
    proc    also covers PRIV_SYSCTL_MEMLOCK

Review the categories named in autodo.conf if you rely on them; scope
"all" is unchanged.
EOM
}
]
